Dan Patlansky and many more.','https://www.citizen.co.za/highway-mail/uncategorized/2015/02/24/sas-hottest-acts-to-perform-at-splashy-fen/']
]
let news=[
  ["07 May 2012","News","Beast debut at The Assembly","Bizcommunity — One of the earliest contemporary notices of BEAST documents the Cape Town debut at The Assembly and introduces the original line-up: Louis Nel and Rian Zietsman of Taxi Violence, Sasha Righini of The Plastics and Lark vocalist Inge Beckmann.","One of the earliest contemporary notices of BEAST documents the Cape Town debut at The Assembly and introduces the original line-up: Louis Nel and Rian Zietsman of Taxi Violence, Sasha Righini of The Plastics and Lark vocalist Inge Beckmann. Source: https://www.bizcommunity.com/Article/196/429/74755.html"],
  ["10 Jul 2012","Feature","BEAST: A Band Apart","One Small Seed — An early profile of the newly formed Cape Town project, cited in later band histories as one of the first substantial pieces on BEAST and its unconventional two-bass approach.","An early profile of the newly formed Cape Town project, cited in later band histories as one of the first substantial pieces on BEAST and its unconventional two-bass approach. Source: https://www.onesmallseed.com/"],
  ["22 Jul 2012","Interview / Feature","Inge Beckmann describes BEAST as the polar opposite of Lark","Evan Milton — In a feature on Lark, Beckmann discusses her then-new dual-bass project BEAST, describing it as a local super-project with members of Taxi Violence and The Plastics and as the polar opposite of Lark.","In a feature on Lark, Beckmann discusses her then-new dual-bass project BEAST, describing it as a local super-project with members of Taxi Violence and The Plastics and as the polar opposite of Lark. Source: https://evanmilton.wordpress.com/2012/07/22/lark-inge-beckmann-and-paul-ressel-are-back/"],
  ["05 Feb 2013","Album Review","BEAST — Smoke Swig Swear","Gevaaalik — A contemporary review focuses on what made the debut unusual in South African rock: no guitars, two bassists, drums and a powerful vocalist, praising the simplicity and originality of the resulting sound.","A contemporary review focuses on what made the debut unusual in South African rock: no guitars, two bassists, drums and a powerful vocalist, praising the simplicity and originality of the resulting sound. Source: https://gevaaalik.com/beast-smoke-swig-swear"],
  ["12 Feb 2013","Profile","Beast: no boundaries","Design Indaba — Design Indaba profiles BEAST around its 2013 Music Circuit appearance, highlighting the band's 'no boundaries' ethos and an organic approach designed to leave room for all four musicians to improvise.","Design Indaba profiles BEAST around its 2013 Music Circuit appearance, highlighting the band's 'no boundaries' ethos and an organic approach designed to leave room for all four musicians to improvise. Source: https://www.designindaba.com/tags/beast"],
  ["27 Feb 2013","Live Review","Raucous rock at Aces n Spades","Design Indaba — Design Indaba's report from its Music Circuit describes a packed Aces n Spades and singles BEAST out as the act the crowd had come to see, documenting the band's rapidly growing Cape Town live reputation.","Design Indaba's report from its Music Circuit describes a packed Aces n Spades and singles BEAST out as the act the crowd had come to see, documenting the band's rapidly growing Cape Town live reputation. Source: https://www.designindaba.com/articles/design-indaba-news/raucous-rock-aces-n-spades"],
  ["22 Mar 2013","Video / Feature","The Jack Daniel's Music Reporter featuring Cape Town band BEAST","2oceansvibe — A video feature introduces BEAST to a wider audience through the members' established Cape Town bands, emphasizing the two-bass/no-guitar setup and Beckmann's commanding vocals.","A video feature introduces BEAST to a wider audience through the members' established Cape Town bands, emphasizing the two-bass/no-guitar setup and Beckmann's commanding vocals. Source: https://www.2oceansvibe.com/2013/03/22/the-jack-daniels-music-reporter-featuring-cape-town-band-beast-video/"],
  ["24 Aug 2013","Album Review","The BEAST With Two Bassists — Smoke Swig Swear","Kurt Writes Things — A detailed review reconstructs the band's origin: Rian Zietsman and Louis Nel deciding they both wanted to learn bass, bringing in Sasha Righini, and developing the idea into the dark garage-rock experiment that became BEAST.","A detailed review reconstructs the band's origin: Rian Zietsman and Louis Nel deciding they both wanted to learn bass, bringing in Sasha Righini, and developing the idea into the dark garage-rock experiment that became BEAST. Source: https://www.kurtwritesthings.com/things/2013/08/the-beast-with-two-bassists-smoke-swig-swear-album-review"],
  ["28 Aug 2013","Premiere / Interview","Premiere: Watch BEAST's video for Smoke Swig Swear","VICE / Noisey — VICE premiered the title-track video internationally, interviewed Inge Beckmann and presented a short documentary about BEAST's rehearsals, recording and album launch. The feature describes the band as a two-bassist, no-guitar quartet mixing rock, punk and grunge.","VICE premiered the title-track video internationally, interviewed Inge Beckmann and presented a short documentary about BEAST's rehearsals, recording and album launch. The feature describes the band as a two-bassist, no-guitar quartet mixing rock, punk and grunge. Source: https://www.vice.com/en/article/premiere-watch-beasts-video-for-smoke-swig-swear/"],
  ["21 Feb 2015","Live / Photography","Bardo exclusive acoustic launch at the Cape Town Club","Laura McCullagh — A photo report documents BEAST's intimate acoustic Bardo launch for supporters at the Cape Town Club, noting how the restrained arrangement intensified the band's music and Beckmann's performance.","A photo report documents BEAST's intimate acoustic Bardo launch for supporters at the Cape Town Club, noting how the restrained arrangement intensified the band's music and Beckma